else:
  print("You foolishly decide to not bring anything with you, a choice that quickly leads to your death. (Ending 1/12)")


print("Looking around, it is dimly lit, with torches hanging against the wall.")
print("You hear sudden sounds, almost like footsteps coming from a nearby corridor, what do you do?")
print("1) ""You follow the sound of footsteps, coming across a massive door standing in your way.")
print("2) ""You decide against following them and continue forward, ending up meeting a swarm of monsters.")
choice = input("What do you do?")

if not choice.isdigit():
  print("You are impaled by a spike trap in the wall. You died. (Ending 2/12)")

elif int(choice) == 1:
  print("You push open the door and come face to face with a seemingly empty throne in the middle of the room.")
  print("You look around but the princess is nowhere in sight, so you turn to leave before feeling a chilling presence. The monster that rules over this dungeon has entered the same room, blocking the exit for you.")
  print("No matter the decision you could have made, the monster was too strong for you, swallowing you whole. (Ending 3/12)")
  
elif int(choice) == 2:
  print("As you come upon the swarm of monsters, they close in on you as you ready yourself to fight.")
  if has_shield:
    print("You are able to defend yourself for a while, but with no weapon to fight with, you are eventually overwhelmed and slained by the monsters. (Ending 4/12)")
  if has_sword:
    print("You are able to mow down the swarm of monsters, but not without sustaining injuries, some which are severe. You leave the dungeon, failing in your mission (Ending 5/12)")
  if has_sword_and_shield:
    print("You are able to clear the swarm of monsters with little problem and push on further along the long and dark corridor")

print("You push on, hearing the panicked cries from the princess, eventually bringing you to another fork in the dungeon, this time with 3 different doors.")
print("The first door is a plain ordinary door.")
print("The second one is grotesquely ornate, with a large golden outline and jeweled doorhandle.")
print("The third and final door is a clean slate of marble, which you can hear the princess' cries coming from the other side.")
print("Which door do you choose to go through?")
choice = input("Where do you go?")

if not choice.isdigit():
  print("You decide against going to any of them and turn around to go somewhere else, leading to your permanent disappearnce through unknown means. (Ending 6/12)")

elif int(choice) == 1:
  print("You push open the first door, which is where the princess was actually residing, which makes you realize those cries were a trap that a demon had placed in order to lure you to your death.")

elif int(choice) == 2:
  print("You head to the ornate door, but to your shock and disgust, it opens up into a mouth and bites you in two, before taking its long prehensile tongue and swallowing both parts of you. (Ending 7/12)")

elif int(choice) == 3:
 print("You push open the marble door, expecting to see the princess on the other side, but you instead see a demon that impales you with his trident, letting you bleed out. (Ending 8/12)")

print("You quickly take the princess out of the room, defending her when any monsters come up, but suddenly a influx of magic permeates the hallway, and a large, 4-legged monster appears from the shadows")
print("Do you flee or guard the princess?")
print("1) You take the princess and run as far as you can towards the exit.")
print("2) You ready yourself to fight the monster, even as you know you likely won't win.")
choice = input("What do you do?")

if not choice.isdigit():
  print("You freeze in place due to horror and let the monster thrash both you and the princess, leaving you two lifeless. (Ending 9/12)")

elif int(choice) == 1:
  print("You flee with the princess, successfully bringing her out of the dungeon and back to the castle. (Ending 10/12)")

elif int(choice) == 2:
  print("You ready your weapon, ready to defend the princess with your life.")
  if has_shield:
    print("All you can do is defend with your shield, which gives the princess enough time to defend, but leaves you with life-threatening injuries, and you fall unconcious from a vicious blow to your head. (Ending 11/12)")
  if has_sword:
    print("You're able to successfully fend off the monster, but you are seriously injured, but still able to make it out of the dungeon. (Ending 12/12)")
